How do you generate a sequence of dates (date range) in SQL?
Use a recursive CTE to generate a date series, or a numbers table joined with DATEADD. In
PostgreSQL/BigQuery, GENERATE_SERIES() provides this natively. Date ranges are essential for filling
gaps in time-series data, building calendars, and ensuring continuous date sequences in reporting pipelines.

-- PostgreSQL: generate dates for Jan 2024
SELECT generate_series(
'2024-01-01'::date,
'2024-01-31'::date,
'1 day'::interval
)::date AS dt;

-- Recursive CTE (universal)
WITH RECURSIVE dates AS (
SELECT '2024-01-01'::date AS dt
UNION ALL SELECT dt + 1 FROM dates WHERE dt < '2024-01-31'
)
SELECT dt FROM dates;
